  "summary": {
    "plain": "While MiniCLEAN was being cooled, the collaboration measured how long the slow component of argon scintillation lasts in cold argon gas, finding the longest value ever reported, a sign of very pure argon.",
    "technical": "Triplet lifetime of the scintillation light in cold gaseous argon (below 140 K, about 1.5 bar) from the February-April 2017 cold-gas run; the paper also studies the quenching of separate scintillation components."
